<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="chrysoeriol biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-6232" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Arabidopsis thaliana col&lt;/i&gt;: Enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Arabidopsis thaliana col. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; Flavonoids are a highly diverse class of plant secondary metabolites (with over 9000 compounds identified so far |CITS: [16137727]|) synthesized by the phenylpropanoid pathway. They exhibit a wide range of biological functions in higher plants. They are involved in UV protection, flower coloration, and antimicrobial defense |CITS: [11130659]|. They also exhibit antioxidant and anticancer properties |CITS: [12224601][18645020]|. Chrysoeriol is a flavonoid with antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties |CITS: [16450301]|. Chrysoeriol has also been shown to function as a signal molecule and induce the transcription of nodulation (&lt;i&gt;nod&lt;/i&gt;) genes in |FRAME:TAX-382| |CITS: [16667231]|.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="PMN" />
    <Author name="zhang" />
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
